# SwiftFormat configuration for Rivulet.
#
# Philosophy: tuned to the code that already exists, not to SwiftFormat's
# defaults. Running the defaults rewrites 344/380 files because they fight the
# repo's established style (heavy explicit `self`, unsorted imports, one-line
# bodies, mixed trailing commas). This config keeps the rules that are genuine
# cleanups (indentation, redundant returns, dead code) and DISABLES the rules
# that would only churn the tree to impose a different-but-equal style.
#
# Options below were derived from `swiftformat --inferoptions Rivulet` so the
# formatter agrees with the code instead of reformatting it. SwiftFormat owns
# formatting; SwiftLint (see .swiftlint.yml) owns correctness — the two do not
# overlap. Enforced locally via pre-commit on changed files, so the residual
# normalizes incrementally as files are touched rather than in one mega-diff.
#
# Residual first-run churn with this config: 122 files (vs 344 on defaults).
# Re-measure after any change:  swiftformat . --lint

--swiftversion 6.0

# --- Style options matched to the existing tree (from --inferoptions) ---
--indent 4
--ifdef no-indent               # bodies of #if are not extra-indented here
--pattern-let inline            # `if case let .x(y)` not `if case .x(let y)`
--strip-unused-args closure-only
--no-space-operators ...,..<    # `0...9`, `0..<9` written tight in this repo

# --- Rules disabled because they impose a different style, not a fix ---
# Each of these rewrites 40-160 files with no correctness gain.
--disable redundantSelf         # the repo writes explicit self deliberately
--disable sortImports           # import order is left to the author
--disable consecutiveSpaces     # would collapse intentional alignment
--disable blankLinesAtStartOfScope, blankLinesBetweenScopes, blankLinesAroundMark
--disable unusedArguments        # renaming to _ hurts protocol-method readability
--disable andOperator            # `&&` is clearer than a comma in this codebase
--disable docComments            # do not force // comments into /// doc comments
--disable conditionalAssignment  # leave if/switch-expression assignment to the author
--disable initCoderUnavailable   # UIKit views here manage required init(coder:) by hand
--disable preferKeyPath          # `map { $0.x }` is fine; not worth the churn
--disable trailingCommas         # the tree is mixed; enforcing either way is pure churn

# Body/brace wrapping: the repo uses one-line bodies (`if x { return }`); the
# default wrap-body rules would explode those across the whole tree.
--disable wrapMultilineStatementBraces, wrapArguments
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies, wrapFunctionBodies, wrapPropertyBodies, wrapLoopBodies

# Test-hygiene rules that make SEMANTIC edits (foo! -> try XCTUnwrap(foo),
# adding `throws`). A formatter should not rewrite test logic.
--disable noForceUnwrapInTests, noForceTryInTests

# redundantOptionalBinding (`if let x = x` -> `if let x`) is a fine modernization
# but touches 27 files; skip it to keep the first-run diff small.
--disable redundantOptionalBinding

--exclude Rivulet/OpenSourceLicenses.swift, Rivulet/Config/Secrets.swift, node_modules, .wrangler, DerivedData, .build, RivuletTests/Fixtures
